    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Newell grew around a massive glass manufacturing plant that opened in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/newell-146817"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s name honors the Newell family, early settlers who helped establish the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/newell-146817"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Newell lies in southwestern Pennsylvania, an area historically rich in coal, coke, and glass production, within the greater Pittsburgh metropolitan influence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/newell-146817"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The United States Glass Company once ran a major factory in Newell that employed many locals for decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/newell-146817"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Even after the plant closed, Newell’s streets and buildings still echo its manufacturing heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/newell-146817"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Newell borders only Jefferson Township to the east, while the Monongahela River separates it from Washington County towns across the water.",
